          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "min by (job) (up{namespace=\"monitoring\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Observability targets",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Every Prometheus target in the monitoring namespace, one tile per job. Selected by namespace rather than by job name on purpose: the job label is derived from each chart's Service name and would break silently if a chart were renamed.\n\nExpect Prometheus, Alertmanager, kube-state-metrics, node-exporter, Tempo and the OTel collector. Loki may be absent entirely \u2014 gitops/platform/loki/values-kind.yaml does not enable a ServiceMonitor, so a missing Loki tile means nothing is scraping it, not that it is down. Judge Loki by whether the logs panels on the service dashboards return lines."
    },
